<title>INDIA: Nestle India 1996 net 528 mln rupees.</title>
<headline>Nestle India 1996 net 528 mln rupees.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		 528  vs    416</p>
<p>    Net sales	     12,048  vs  9,963</p>
<p>    Other income		96  vs    48</p>
<p>    Total expenditure   10,801  vs 8,828</p>
<p>    Interest costs	   506  vs   315</p>
<p>    Depreciation	     227  vs   165</p>
<p>    Tax			   68  vs   171</p>
<p>    Extraordinary item	14  vs   116</p>
<p>NOTE: Food and beverage firm Nestle India Ltd, a unit of Switzerland's Nestle SA, said in a statement that it exported 2.51 billion rupees' worth of products in 1996.</p>
<p>It paid two interim dividends of 2.50 rupees and 2.00 rupees in 1996, the second interim dividend being on enhanced capital after the issue of bonus shares.</p>
<p>It said a new culinary products factory in the western state of Goa will be commissioned shortly.</p>
<p>--  New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
